# Embedded UI (`external/ui`)

- Start with [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md). Read only the relevant contract: [foundations](../../specs/ui/foundations.md), [layout](../../specs/ui/layout.md), [composer](../../specs/ui/composer.md), [transcript](../../specs/ui/transcript.md), [settings](../../specs/ui/settings.md), [workspace](../../specs/ui/workspace.md), or [components](../../specs/ui/components.md). Consult [implementation notes](../../specs/ui/implementation.md) for file ownership, state and regression tests. Update the owning spec when behavior changes.
- Keep the SCSS cascade in `src/styles.scss`, shared tokens in `_tokens.scss`, palettes in `themes/`, and component styles in their surface partial. Keep simplified mode last. Use theme tokens instead of hardcoded accents.
- Update all registered locale dictionaries together when user-facing copy changes. Keep browser geometry checks in a real browser as specified by the paired UI verification rule.
- Format touched SPA files with Prettier (`make ui-format-check` verifies the tree). After changing shipped UI sources, run `make build TAGS="http ui"` to rebuild embedded assets.
- Keep optimistic draft clearing reversible until the server accepts the turn. A failed send restores text and attachments and preserves the underlying error where safe.
